---
import { BOOKING_URL } from '../data/site';
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import Panel from '../components/Panel.astro';
---
<Site
  title="Services: process audit and AI implementation | DNA4Digital"
  description="I usually start with an audit of your sales process. Then I train your team on its own data and build the automations. If you need software, Yameo builds it."
>
  <Panel rung={0} kicker="01 · Services">
    <h1>I usually start with an audit. We decide the rest after it.</h1>
    <p class="lead">First I look at how work moves through your company, from first contact to invoice. I build the automations myself and train your team on its own data.</p>
    <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <a href="#gtm">GTM &amp; processes</a><a href="#training">Training</a><a href="#audit">Audits</a><a href="#consulting">Consulting</a><a href="#delivery">After the audit</a>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="gtm">Go-to-market and the processes underneath it</h2>
    <p>GTM is where I'm strongest, and where I see the most AI money thrown away. Teams usually start with what they can see: AI drafts their emails and summarises their calls. Meanwhile each person reads the pipeline stages differently, leads wait four days between marketing and sales, the CRM has three fields for the same thing, and nobody has written down what &ldquo;qualified&rdquo; means.</p>
    <p>Automate that and you get the same confusion, only faster. So I first get your sales process clear enough to fit on one page, then add AI to the steps your team repeats most.</p>
    <div class="pcards">
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Sales process map</h3><p>I draw the whole customer path through to signature and renewal: the stages, what moves a deal on, who owns each step, and where deals fall between people.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Funnel and CRM cleanup</h3><p>Qualification rules the whole team shares, and forecasts leadership can trust. The CRM keeps only the fields people fill in.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>GTM automation</h3><p>Research, enrichment, lead routing, follow-ups, call notes and reports. I build them on a process that already works, so the time savings last.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Training for sales and service teams</h3><p>I train SDRs, AEs, marketing and customer service to work in the new process, on your data and your live deals.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="callout"><p>At the end you get a process map with the problems ranked by cost, and a 90-day plan in two columns: &ldquo;fix in the process&rdquo; and &ldquo;automate&rdquo;.</p></div>

    <h2 id="training">Training and workshops</h2>
    <p>I fit each programme to the roles and processes in your company. People practise on their own data and tasks, so they can use AI in their work the same week.</p>
    <div class="pcards three">
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Marketing &amp; sales</h3><p>Ready-made workflows for pipeline, content, research, analytics and CRM work. We practise on the leads in your pipeline today.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Operations &amp; admin</h3><p>Document standards and tidied-up procedures. Then quality control and automation for the repetitive steps.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>HR &amp; knowledge</h3><p>Onboarding, knowledge bases, policies and SOPs where a new starter can find the answer on their own.</p></div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="audit">Audits</h2>
    <p>I review your processes and data and look for the places where an AI investment will pay back fastest. In the implementation plan, each step has its own metric, baseline and deadline.</p>
    <p>After the audit workshop you know where to start, and you have a process map with tool recommendations.</p>
    <div class="btnrow">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={BOOKING_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book an audit call</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/ai-readiness/">Take the AI readiness test</a>
    </div>

    <h2 id="consulting">Consulting</h2>
    <p>I see an AI rollout through to the end. I choose the first automations for the time they save your team. Then I build AI assistants and knowledge bases around how your team works today, and write down the standards so your people can use them without me.</p>
    <div class="pcards three">
      <div class="pcard"><h3>First automations</h3><p>I find where your team loses the most time and build the first automations there.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>AI assistants</h3><p>Prompts, usage rules and integrations, built so you can audit them later.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Knowledge base &amp; SOPs</h3><p>Documents, policies and checklists in one place, current and easy to find.</p></div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="delivery">After the audit</h2>
    <p>We start with an audit: a process map and a list of what costs you most. The next step depends on what the audit shows.</p>
    <p><strong>If fixing the process and configuration is enough</strong>, I do it myself in a few weeks: automations, CRM, SOPs, dashboards and team training. I set it up to run without me.</p>
    <p><strong>If you need software written</strong>, Yameo joins the project. It's a Dutch-Polish software house that has built systems for banking, insurance and healthcare since 2006, and I'm an Associate Partner there. I stay on the project and answer for whether the system solves your problem. You deal with me throughout, and Yameo only builds what configuration can't handle.</p>
    <div class="pcards">
      <div class="pcard">
        <h3>I do this myself (DNA4Digital)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>GTM and revenue process design</li>
          <li>Process mapping, SOPs, KPIs</li>
          <li>AI readiness audits and implementation plans</li>
          <li>Low-code automation (n8n, Zapier, HubSpot)</li>
          <li>Team training</li>
          <li>Dashboards and reporting (Looker Studio)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="pcard">
        <h3>With the Yameo team</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Custom software and platform builds</li>
          <li>System integrations and migrations at scale</li>
          <li>Projects in regulated industries</li>
          <li>Anything needing an engineering team for months</li>
          <li>Fixed-price, fixed-date, SLA-backed delivery</li>
          <li>Long-term development partnership</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Start with a 30-minute call</h2>
    <p>The call is free and online. At the end I'll tell you where I would start.</p>
    <div class="btnrow"><a class="btn btn-primary" href={BOOKING_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a free consultation</a></div>
  </Panel>
</Site>
